From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirill =?UTF-8?q?M=C3=BCller?= <kirill@cynkra.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Tell a database still in use from a shutdown in flight

DBInstanceCache::GetInstanceInternal() finds a cache entry whose DuckDB
handle is gone, concludes that a shutdown is in flight on another thread,
and busy-spins until the entry expires. ~DatabaseInstance releases the
entry on its last line, so when a shutdown really is in flight that takes
microseconds and the reasoning holds.

It is not the only way to reach that state. A DatabaseInstance can
outlive the DuckDB handle that pointed at it: a ClientContext holds a
DatabaseInstance, and a connection or an unfinished result holds a
ClientContext. Release the last DuckDB handle while either is alive and
the entry stays with a null handle and no shutdown running to finish it.
The spin then never terminates, at 100% CPU, with no interrupt check to
break out of -- in a single-threaded embedding such as R, a wedge that
Ctrl-C does not reach.

The entry gains a weak_ptr to the instance, and that is what tells the
two cases apart: an instance that still locks is not being destroyed, so
nothing will ever release the entry and waiting for it is futile. The
wait is bounded on both sides -- 100 ms before a live instance is
reported as still in use, 5 seconds before a shutdown that never finishes
is reported as such -- and the first message says whether connections are
open, because ~Connection deregisters while an unfinished result does
not, so a count of zero names the result.

The grace period is load-bearing rather than defensive. ~DuckDB drops the
handle before it drops the instance, so a shutdown that is genuinely in
flight also presents as a live instance with no handle; reporting that
immediately turned 4 of 200 concurrent close-and-reopen rounds into
spurious errors, and 100 ms takes that to 0. Measured in
experiments/2026-09-19-instance-cache-in-use/.

Reporting rather than falling through to CreateInstance is deliberate:
the file lock does not fire within one process, so creating would succeed
and leave two instances writing one file, each blind to what the other
commits.

Proposed upstream in duckdb/duckdb#26134 against v1.5-variegata, staged
in krlmlr/duckdb#200 (main), #201 (v1.5-variegata) and #202
(v2.0-cyanoptera), and carried here until a release carries it.
The region it touches is identical on all three, so it is one patch; the
file as a whole is not, because v2.0-cyanoptera carries a
CreateEmptyInstance() that main and v1.5-variegata do not.
---
diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/main/db_instance_cache.hpp b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/main/db_instance_cache.hpp
index a8a14c41..3206b7f5 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/main/db_instance_cache.hpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/main/db_instance_cache.hpp
@@ -23,6 +23,9 @@ struct DatabaseCacheEntry {
 	~DatabaseCacheEntry();
 
 	weak_ptr<DuckDB> database;
+	//! The instance behind that handle: it outlives the handle whenever a ClientContext still holds it,
+	//! which is how an entry with no handle can still be in use rather than shutting down
+	weak_ptr<DatabaseInstance> instance;
 	mutex update_database_mutex;
 };
 
diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/main/db_instance_cache.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/main/db_instance_cache.cpp
index c774ba86..80e3a82b 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/main/db_instance_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/main/db_instance_cache.cpp
@@ -1,9 +1,17 @@
 #include "duckdb/main/db_instance_cache.hpp"
 #include "duckdb/main/extension_helper.hpp"
 #include "duckdb/main/database_file_path_manager.hpp"
+#include "duckdb/common/chrono.hpp"
+#include "duckdb/parallel/task_scheduler.hpp"
 
 namespace duckdb {
 
+//! How long to wait for an in-flight shutdown before reporting that the database is still in use
+static constexpr int64_t SHUTDOWN_WAIT_SECONDS = 5;
+
+//! How long a shutdown is given to finish before a live instance is reported as still in use
+static constexpr int64_t IN_USE_GRACE_MILLIS = 100;
+
 DatabaseCacheEntry::DatabaseCacheEntry() {
 }
 
@@ -78,11 +86,47 @@ shared_ptr<DuckDB> DBInstanceCache::GetInstanceInternal(const string &database,
 	}
 	// cache entry exists - check if the actual database still exists
 	if (!db_instance) {
-		// if the database does not exist, but the cache entry still exists, the database is being shut down
-		// we need to wait until the database is fully shut down to safely proceed
-		// we do this here using a busy spin
+		// an entry whose handle is gone is usually a shutdown finishing, which takes microseconds. but a
+		// DatabaseInstance can outlive that handle, because a ClientContext holds one and a connection or an
+		// unfinished result holds a ClientContext - then nothing is shutting down, the entry is released on
+		// the last line of ~DatabaseInstance and never expires, and waiting for it is futile
+		//
+		// we report rather than fall through to CreateInstance: the file lock does not fire within a single
+		// process, so creating would succeed and leave two instances writing the same file
 		cache_entry.reset();
+		auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+		// the grace period is what keeps a shutdown that is genuinely in flight from being reported as in
+		// use: ~DuckDB drops the handle before it drops the instance, so the instance is briefly alive
+		// while a real shutdown runs
+		auto grace = now + std::chrono::milliseconds(IN_USE_GRACE_MILLIS);
+		auto deadline = now + std::chrono::seconds(SHUTDOWN_WAIT_SECONDS);
 		while (!weak_cache_entry.expired()) {
+			TaskScheduler::YieldThread();
+			now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+			if (now > grace) {
+				auto entry = weak_cache_entry.lock();
+				shared_ptr<DatabaseInstance> live_instance;
+				if (entry) {
+					live_instance = entry->instance.lock();
+				}
+				entry.reset();
+				if (live_instance) {
+					auto connections = ConnectionManager::Get(*live_instance).GetConnectionCount();
+					live_instance.reset();
+					if (connections > 0) {
+						throw ConnectionException("Database \"%s\" is still in use: %llu connection(s) are open on it",
+						                          database, connections);
+					}
+					throw ConnectionException("Database \"%s\" is still in use: no connections are open, but "
+					                          "something still holds it, such as an unfinished query result",
+					                          database);
+				}
+				grace = now + std::chrono::milliseconds(IN_USE_GRACE_MILLIS);
+			}
+			if (now > deadline) {
+				throw ConnectionException("Database \"%s\" did not finish shutting down within %d seconds", database,
+				                          SHUTDOWN_WAIT_SECONDS);
+			}
 		}
 		D_ASSERT(!cache_entry);
 		// the cache entry has now been deleted - clear it from the set of database instances and return
@@ -134,6 +178,7 @@ shared_ptr<DuckDB> DBInstanceCache::CreateInstanceInternal(const string &databas
 		db_instances_lock.unlock();
 		db_instance = make_shared_ptr<DuckDB>(instance_path, &config);
 		cache_entry->database = db_instance;
+		cache_entry->instance = db_instance->instance;
 	} else {
 		db_instances_lock.unlock();
 		db_instance = make_shared_ptr<DuckDB>(instance_path, &config);
